 { Bearing the previous example in mind, it is not difficult to spot Black's best defence here. } 1... { -KEY- } Rb6 $1 { Preventing the advance of the enemy king. } 2. e6 ( { The only way to try and progress; e.g. } 2. Rg7 Ra6 3. Rg6 { is useless due to } Rxg6 4. Kxg6 Ke7 ) 
Rb1 $1 ( { The same procedure as before - once } 2... Rb1 2. Kf6 { is a threat, the rook prepares a rear attack. This two-step method, waiting on the sixth rank until the pawn advances and then launching a rear attack with the rook, was discovered by Philidor. His method keeps great importance in practice, as we will see in a few later examples in this section. } ) 
3. Kf6 Rf1+ 4. Ke5 Re1+ 5. Kd6 Rd1+ { Draw. } 
