 { White's plan is evident: help the b-pawn with his king. The fact that Black's king has been cut off from the queenside means that only a frontal attack can save him. } 1... { -KEY- } Rb8 $1 { To the edge, increasing the rook's range as a preparation for the frontal attack. } 2. Kc3 Rc8+ 3. Kb2 Rb8 $1 4. Re4 { White renews the threat of b3-b4, but in so doing leaves the third rank, a fact that Black immediately exploits. } Rf8 $1 5. Re3 ( { Obviously, } 5. b4 Rf3 6. b5 Rxg3 7. b6 Rf3 { is nothing for White. } ) 
