 { In the current position, Black's problem is that he can't bring his king out without permitting a white rook check. However, a clever rook manoeuvre could have solved this problem. } 1... { -KEY- } Rd2+ $1 { The rook is transferred to the seventh rank, to serve as a shield for the king. } ( { Instead, the game went } 1... Kb1 $2 2. Rb8 $1 Rxh7 { and Black accepted a draw without waiting for 3.Rxb3+. } ) 
2. Ke1 Rd7 3. Ke2 Rc7 ( { a) Similar winning paths are } 3... Ra7 4. Kxe3 Ka2 ) 
 ( { b) And } 3... Re7 4. Kd1 ( { or } 3... Rc7 3. Ke1 e2 { with zugzwang } ) 
Ra7 5. Ke2 Ka2 { - Stohl, 'Chess Today'. } ) 
4. Kxe3 Kc2 { White is helpless against the threat of ...b3-b2. } 
