 { This endgame seems difficult for Black, but a clever rook manoeuvre saved his cause. } 1... { -KEY- } Rf8 $1 2. c7 Rf2+ 3. Ke1 d2+ 4. Kxf2 ( { Not } 4. Kd1 $4 Ke3 $1 { and Black even wins the game. } ) 
d1=Q 5. Re6+ ( { Or } 5. c8=Q $11 Qd2 { with a perpetual. } ) 
Kd3 6. c8=Q Qd2+ $1 ( 6... Qe2 $2 { is well-intended, but } 7. Kg3 $1 { avoids the stalemate trick, as noticed by Vjekoslav. Fortunately, the same idea is still in the air. } ) 
7. Kg1 { It seems like White will escape the perpetual by transferring his king to h3, but Black has a new surprise prepared... } Qc1+ $3 8. Qxc1 { Stalemate. } 
